<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guanabara Bay</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Baía de Guanabara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guanabara Bay is a large bay on the south-eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, on whose shores stand the cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> and Niterói. In 1555 French settlers under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolas-durand-de-villegaignon">Nicolas Durand de Villegaignon</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> Antarctique on an island in the bay. The Portuguese expelled them in 1560–1567 and founded Rio de Janeiro, which grew into the colonial capital of Brazil.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guanabara-bay.jpg" alt="Guanabara Bay" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rio_deJaneiro_LE2002059_lrg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
